    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1235">

                <pb facs="1796" n="1780" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.0081 Conferences/6–1349</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Morocco</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >More</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier, Morocco</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-13">June 13, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 129</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    report on the political items on the agenda of the North African
                        Conference<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1235-f1"/> held at this Legation on June 6,
                    7, 8, 9 and 10, 1949 pursuant to the Department’s instructions. The officers who
                    attended the Conference are listed in Enclosure 1.</p>
                <p>It was my privilege to preside at the opening session, after which Mr. Earl L.
                    Packer, Consul General at Tunis, acted as Chairman. I designated Mr. Albert W.
                    Sherer, Jr., of the Legation, as Drafting Officer and he was greatly assisted by
                    Mr. Ridgway B. Knight, of the Embassy at Paris, as well as by the Chairman and
                    other officers in preparing the report, all sections of which were unanimously
                    approved.</p>
                <p>The Legation’s despatch no. 130 dated June 13, 1949 includes a discussion of the
                    other items on the agenda.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bolard More</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d1235-a1.xml" xpointer="d1235-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d1235-a2.xml" xpointer="d1235-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1235-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1235-f1-content">
                <p>This conference was similar to other regional conferences periodically conducted
                    abroad by the Department of State. For documentation on the Near Eastern
                    regional conference for diplomatic and consular officers held in Istanbul,
                    November 26–29, see <ref target="#pg165">pp. 165</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
